B. EXPLANATIONS
Changed `folder_size_kb` to call `du` via an argument list (`["du", "-sk", folder]`) without `shell=True`. This passes `folder` as a single argv element to `du` directly, so shell metacharacters (`;`, `|`, backticks, `#`, etc.) are never interpreted by a shell — they're just part of the literal path argument. This removes the injection vector while preserving the same return value (parsed integer KB from `du`'s output) for any legitimate path, including paths with spaces.

C. COMPATIBILITY RISK
Low — the output format of `du -sk <path>` is identical whether invoked via shell or exec list; only paths that previously relied on shell expansion (e.g. globs, `~`, env vars) would behave differently, but such usage was unintended/unsafe anyway and not part of the documented function contract.

